## Secure Cryptographic Device Architecture Types ## {#scd-architecture-types}
<!-- Section owner: Rene Leveille -->

<p class="issue">
Placeholder: Expand descriptions of the possible architecture types for the [=Secure Cryptographic Device=].
</p>

- **Remote SCD** — A remote device, such as a Hardware Security Module (HSM), accessed over a network.
- **Local External SCD** — An external device, such as a smart card or secure token, connected to the [=User Device=].
- **Local Internal SCD** — A component embedded within the [=User Device=], such as a SIM, eSIM, or embedded Secure Element.
- **Local Native SCD** — A component embedded in the [=User Device=] and accessed via an API provided by the operating system.

